;
; What Poseidon thinks it has, and what it did about it.
;
; The HCD trace says the mouse enumerates and is then never spoken to again.
; That reading was wrong twice, so state what the driver's own counters
; actually establish: three of them are not per-address and all three are at
; zero across every boot so far -- no SOF service tick, no parked periodic
; NAK, no interrupt data. An interrupt IN transfer has therefore never
; reached the driver at all. The question is not what the DWC2 did with the
; mouse; it is why nothing above ever asked it for the mouse's pipe.
;
; So ask the stack. Run it late, with a finished system, and put every answer
; on DEBUG: where the serial log can carry it.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] --- poseidon.library"
Version >DEBUG: poseidon.library

Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] --- classes present on the card"
List >DEBUG: USBCLASSES: LFORMAT "%N"

Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] --- what AddUSBHardware said at boot"
If EXISTS "SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
    Type >DEBUG: "SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
Else
    Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] no usb-hardware.log -- the block never ran"
EndIf

;
; The Startup-Sequence runs this as `Run <NIL: >NIL: QUIET AddUSBClasses`:
; asynchronous, silent, and with its output on NIL:, so a failure there is
; invisible. Run it again in the foreground with somewhere to speak. It
; prints "Skipping class X" for every class already registered, which is the
; direct answer to whether the first run finished -- and it ends in
; psdClassScan(), so if the first run lost a race with AddUSBHardware this
; second scan is also the cure.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] --- AddUSBClasses again, in the foreground"
AddUSBClasses >DEBUG: *>DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] --- AddUSBClasses returned"

Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] --- the device tree and its bindings"
PsdDevLister >DEBUG: *>DEBUG: SHOWROOT TOPOLOGY

;
; Poseidon narrates itself through psdAddErrorMsg: hub.class writes "New
; device '%s' at port %ld" for every device it configures, and every failure
; on the way there writes a line too. NOFLUSH keeps the log for anything that
; reads it later.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] --- poseidon's own error log"
PsdErrorlog >DEBUG: *>DEBUG: NOFLUSH
Echo >DEBUG: "[usb-report] --- end"
